1
00:00:00,830 --> 00:00:02,490
Why does your
computer need a fan?

2
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:05,470
The heat comes from
somewhere you can't see.

3
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:09,450
Inside the chip are billions
of tiny switches, called

4
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:10,330
transistors.

5
00:00:11,230 --> 00:00:14,030
They flip on and off,
up to billions of times

6
00:00:14,030 --> 00:00:16,670
a second, whenever your
computer does anything at

7
00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:17,470
all.

8
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:20,690
Each flip takes a tiny
bit of electricity.

9
00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:23,030
On its own, that's nothing.

10
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:26,710
But billions of switches,
billions of times a second,

11
00:00:27,130 --> 00:00:27,570
add up.

12
00:00:27,570 --> 00:00:30,590
And that electricity doesn't
get stored away anywhere.

13
00:00:31,430 --> 00:00:33,130
Almost all of it
ends up as heat.

14
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:36,130
So the fan, the metal
fins and the little pipes

15
00:00:36,130 --> 00:00:38,470
are there to carry it
away, before the chip has

16
00:00:38,470 --> 00:00:39,590
to slow itself down.

17
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:43,130
When your fan spins up, that's
the sound of arithmetic.
